                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Wikiholic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7e253cc-d098-3e42-85dc-e121e474bf20",
                                        "entry_id": "fb539473-40b2-34ee-98ca-5478343d5706",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who is addicted to editing Wikipedia or another wiki."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13a11131-cc7c-4cb3-bb41-799d8236edb8",
                                                "sense_id": "e7e253cc-d098-3e42-85dc-e121e474bf20",
                                                "text": "I'm a Wikipedia editor. A Wikiholic. I have some 500 articles on my watchlist (!!!) and I edit some of the more controversial articles on WP: the Islam-related articles. For many months, I have been butting heads with some Iranian Shi'a editors..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef4dfcfe-fe02-41a8-8286-a622a24ccdcb",
                                                "sense_id": "e7e253cc-d098-3e42-85dc-e121e474bf20",
                                                "text": "2005, Richard Quinn, as quoted by David Dyer-Bennet, “Re: Charlie Stross: Wikipedian Extraordinaire” (April 8), rec.arts.sf.written, Usenet\nI was blessed with insight, that rare moment of lucidity which can truly validate the Buddhist belief in a path to enlightenment: Charles Stross is a Wikiholic!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0935cde-120f-4f06-9c76-f3adfb2ceecb",
                                                "sense_id": "e7e253cc-d098-3e42-85dc-e121e474bf20",
                                                "text": "\"A lot of them are probably the sort of people who would have social problems in real life,\" said one wikimaniac over lunch, as though being a \"wikiholic\" suggested a full and active life."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "168b810d-9c39-4928-83bd-61b3af9c7aa7",
                        "source_entry_id": "3b850cd4-1b89-3513-9146-b0ecc0e25f94",
                        "source_sense_id": "58318ae4-80d8-3429-b182-e6424963f810",
                        "target_lang_word": "Wikipediholism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Wikipediholism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7adf6b6-748b-33ae-8797-b37ffcc44815",
                                        "entry_id": "ce528230-7233-3a95-a2a9-885229a0d67b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An addiction to editing Wikipedia."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90ac04d8-8fa1-4d2d-b12d-6889cd0b0a34",
                                                "sense_id": "e7adf6b6-748b-33ae-8797-b37ffcc44815",
                                                "text": "Blog streaking, Google-stalking, Wikipediholism and other modern maladies"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7c4a614-4aa8-45d0-b155-89be00aa388c",
                                                "sense_id": "e7adf6b6-748b-33ae-8797-b37ffcc44815",
                                                "text": "The author of the original tool for counting edits noted that editcountitis, or an unhealthy obsession with the notion of edit count, can be fatal. Editcountitis is often a symptom of Wikipediholism, which is an even worse disease. The only sure treatment is worrying more about the quality of your edits than the quantity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03b3d95f-eb46-4518-895c-4c0d92847639",
                                                "sense_id": "e7adf6b6-748b-33ae-8797-b37ffcc44815",
                                                "text": "The community has dubbed obsessively editing the encyclopedia Wikipediholism; an article for the term warns that, \"like any behavioral addiction, Wikipedia overuse may lead to job loss, divorce, bankruptcy, or worse. […] Remember, it's your time and you are donating it to Wikipedia. It is healthy to donate what you can afford to donate, but no more.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
